==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*leuganą}}. Cognates with Old English {{m|ang|lēoġan}} (Modern English {{m|en|lie}}), Old Saxon {{m|osx|liogan}}, Dutch {{m|nl|liegen}}, Old High German {{m|goh|liogan}} (German {{m|de|lügen}}), Gothic {{m|got|𐌻𐌹𐌿𐌲𐌰𐌽}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{m|ine-pro|*lewgʰ-}}. Indo-European cognates include Lithuanian {{m|lt|lūgoti}}.

===Verb===
{{non-verb}}

# to [[lie]], to tell [[lies]]

